      en: "Diamantina is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Brazil. A historic colonial town that grew rich from diamond mining in the 18th and 19th centuries. UNESCO World Heritage site. Center of diamond mining. Birthplace of Juscelino Kubitschek. This site holds particular significance in the history of Brazil, from the Portuguese colonial era to the modern republic. Like many notable places in Brazil, it combines regional character with the wider significance of the world's fifth-largest country. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Brazil, where tropical nature, Portuguese heritage, samba, football, and Carnival come together."
